## Entry for the Table of Contents
An anthracene-based fluorescent linker and a hemicyanine-containing ${\mathsf{C N}}^{-}$ responsive linker were sequentially installed into tailored sites within the lattice of PCN-700. The close proximity and periodic arrangement of the anthracene and hemicyanine linkers facilitated efficient energy transfer between the two components, causing efficient fluorescent quenching. The selective binding of CN- to hemicyanine inhibited the energy transfer between the two moieties, resulting in a fluorescence “turn on” effect.
